<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dominique de Gourgues</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1530–<a href="/years/1593">1593</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dominique de Gourgues was a French soldier from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>. In 1568, to avenge the Spanish massacre of the Huguenot colonists of Fort Caroline in 1565, he led a privately financed expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, where, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timucua">Timucua</a> allies, he captured the Spanish forts on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-johns-river">St Johns River</a> and hanged their garrisons. He returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> without founding a settlement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dominique-de-gourgues.jpg" alt="Dominique de Gourgues" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dominique_de_Gourgues.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Dominique de Gourgues</b> avenged them in 1568, but France did not return, leaving Spanish Florida in control.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-florida">French Florida</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Mont-de-Marsan, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.89,-0.5&amp;year=1570" aria-label="Mont-de-Marsan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4538 609 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Dominique de Gourgues"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4988 879h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4988 879h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.89,-0.5&amp;year=1570">What was here in 1570? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
